ora/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Crystora/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-05-08T17:15:35Z","updated_at":"2026-05-08T17:15:35Z","body":"Sorry for the concern, and thanks for taking the time to look.\r\n\r\nA few quick points:\r\n- The existing `test_astar.cpp` for AStar3D is also a behavior test - builds a graph, asserts a path. This PR mirrors that pattern.\r\n- The error-path tests map directly to `ERR_FAIL_COND` macros in `core/math/a_star.cpp`, which is the documented intent.\r\n- AStar2D has had zero coverage since it was added; tests aren't load-bearing and can be reworked later.\r\n\r\nOn the AI use: I wrote the tests by hand against the AStar3D test and `a_star.cpp`, and only used Claude to polish wording. I've updated the PR description to disclose this.\r\n\r\nWould really appreciate if you'd consider merging \r\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4408394421/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4408480699","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119245#issuecomment-4408480699","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/119245","id":4408480699,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABBsQTuw","user":{"login":"hpvb","id":2591099,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1OTEwOTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2591099?v=4","gra